{"title":"BlueTide Seafood","sub":"Own the trucks, or keep paying a logistics firm?","type":"Investment / capacity","industry":"Food distribution","geo":"United States","diff":3,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Make vs buy · utilisation · hidden costs and benefits","prompt":"BlueTide distributes frozen seafood to restaurants and grocers along the US East Coast. A logistics company (a 3PL) does all its refrigerated trucking for $2.40 a loaded mile. The COO wants to buy BlueTide's own fleet of 40 refrigerated trucks. The CEO asks you whether owning is cheaper, and whether it's the right move.","clarify":[{"q":"Volume?","a":"About 4.4 million loaded miles a year."},{"q":"Fleet costs?","a":"Trucks cost $180k each and last six years. Drivers cost $95k per truck a year. Fuel and maintenance $0.95 a mile. Insurance and admin $0.6M a year."},{"q":"Return trips?","a":"Trucks come back mostly empty: empty miles add about 35% to the loaded miles. The 3PL charges only for loaded miles because it fills return trips with other customers' freight."},{"q":"Could BlueTide sell its empty return capacity?","a":"Probably about half of it, to other shippers, at about $1.60 a mile."},{"q":"Quality?","a":"About 1.2% of cargo value spoils in transit with the 3PL, through temperature failures. BlueTide ships $150M of product a year."}],"structure":{"root":"Should BlueTide run its own fleet?","branches":[{"head":"3PL cost","items":["Loaded miles × rate"]},{"head":"Own-fleet cost","items":["Trucks (depreciation)","Drivers","Fuel and maintenance, including empty miles","Insurance and admin"]},{"head":"Offsets","items":["Selling return capacity","Less spoilage"]},{"head":"Risks","items":["Utilisation","Running a fleet is not our core skill"]}]},"hypothesis":"On loaded miles alone owning looks cheaper, but empty return trips could wipe that out. Spoilage could be the deciding factor, since seafood is valuable.","questions":[{"q":"Compare yearly cost: 3PL vs own fleet, counting only loaded miles.","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>3PL: 4.4M × $2.40 = <b>$10.56M</b>.</p> <p>Own fleet: depreciation $7,200k ÷ 6 = $1.2M; drivers 40 × $95k = $3.8M; fuel and maintenance 4.4M × $0.95 = $4.18M; admin $0.6M. Total <b>$9.78M</b>.</p> <p>Owning looks $0.78M a year cheaper.</p>"},{"q":"Now include the empty return miles.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"378.16pt\" height=\"195.16pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 378.16 195.16\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 195.16 L 378.16 195.16 L 378.16 0 L 0 0 L 0 195.16 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 25 160.16 L 370.96 160.16 L 370.96 10.472 L 25 10.472 L 25 160.16 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"ma99844d2ee\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#ma99844d2ee\" x=\"61.236917\" y=\"160.16\" style=\"fill: #4a5568; stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(45.913792 175.36) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3d\" d=\"M 1184 2573 L 1670 2573 Q 2125 2573 2352 2784 Q 2579 2995 2579 3315 L 2579 3360 Q 2579 3712 2358 3888 Q 2138 4064 1779 4064 Q 1434 4064 1216 3913 Q 998 3763 858 3507 L 461 3814 Q 576 3994 749 4160 Q 922 4326 1178 4435 Q 1434 4544 1792 4544 Q 2170 4544 2477 4413 Q 2784 4282 2966 4032 Q 3149 3782 3149 3418 Q 3149 2989 2899 2726 Q 2650 2464 2291 2374 L 2291 2349 Q 2534 2304 2748 2166 Q 2963 2029 3097 1795 Q 3232 1562 3232 1222 Q 3232 838 3043 547 Q 2854 256 2512 89 Q 2170 -77 1715 -77 Q 1331 -77 1059 35 Q 787 147 598 320 Q 410 493 269 685 L 672 992 Q 845 730 1072 566 Q 1299 403 1709 403 Q 2182 403 2425 620 Q 2669 838 2669 1229 L 26